{
  "abstract": "Let M be the n x n matrix with entries 1/lcm(i,j). R. G. Wilson v conjectured (OEIS A060841, 2015) that 1/det(M) is an integer only for n = 1, ..., 34, 36 and 38. This project proves the conjecture as stated in formal-conjectures (OeisA60841.conjecture1): by Smith's determinant the gcd matrix factors as E diag(phi) E^T with E the unitriangular divisibility matrix, so 1/det(M) = (n!)^2 / prod_{k <= n} phi(k); for n in {1, ..., 34, 36, 38} the divisibility is decided by computation, and for every other n the odd primes up to 97 and the powers of 2 from 4 to 128 force v_2(prod phi(k)) > v_2((n!)^2), numerically for n = 35, 37 and 39 <= n < 100 and by a linear bound for n >= 100.",
  "authors": [
